---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Privacy policy for the IPv6 Council of Zambia website. Learn how we collect, use and protect your personal data."
>
  <div class="c-page-header l-section">
    <div class="l-container">
      <div class="u-badge u-badge--accent">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="c-page-header__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="c-page-header__lead">
        How the IPv6 Council of Zambia collects, uses, and protects your personal information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="l-section">
    <div class="l-container l-container--narrow">
      <div class="c-legal-body l-stack l-stack--lg">

        <div>
          <p class="c-legal-meta">Last updated: November 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            The IPv6 Council of Zambia is a non-profit professional association registered in Zambia. Our website is <strong>https://ipv6zm.org</strong>. If you have any questions about this policy, contact us at <a href={CONTACT.emailMailto}>{CONTACT.email}</a> or call <a href={CONTACT.phoneTel}>{CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
          <p>We may collect the following personal data when you use our website:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — your name, email address, phone number, organisation, and message text.</li>
            <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions</strong> — your email address and, optionally, your name and content preferences.</li>
            <li><strong>Event registrations</strong> — your name, email address, phone number, and organisation.</li>
            <li><strong>Server logs</strong> — your IP address, browser type, pages visited, and timestamps. These are retained for security and performance purposes and are not linked to your identity.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
          <p>We use your personal data solely to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Respond to enquiries you send us.</li>
            <li>Send you newsletters, event announcements, and technical dispatches you subscribed to.</li>
            <li>Process event registrations and workshop bookings.</li>
            <li>Improve the performance and security of this website.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>4. Legal basis for processing</h2>
          <p>
            We process your data on the basis of your consent (for newsletters and contact forms) and our legitimate interest in operating a professional association. You may withdraw consent at any time by contacting us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep contact form data for up to 24 months. Newsletter subscriber data is kept until you unsubscribe. Event registration data is kept for up to 36 months for administrative and reporting purposes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
          <p>You have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
            <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
            <li>Request deletion of your data.</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict processing.</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent at any time.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href={CONTACT.emailMailto}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            This website does not currently use tracking or advertising cookies. We may use a session cookie to remember your form progress. No third-party analytics or advertising scripts are loaded.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last revised. Continued use of the website after a change constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>9. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For any privacy-related enquiries, write to us at <a href={CONTACT.emailMailto}>{CONTACT.email}</a> or call <a href={CONTACT.phoneTel}>{CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .c-page-header {
    background-color: #040404;
    background-image: url('/images/hero-section-background-scaled-1.webp');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center top;
    color: #ffffff;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .c-page-header__title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-h1);
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-block: 0.5rem;
  }

  .c-page-header__lead {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--color-text-inverse-muted);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .c-legal-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .c-legal-body p {
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .c-legal-body ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .c-legal-body a {
    color: var(--color-brand-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .c-legal-meta {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
